--- !u!114 &1380322323227325228
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1380322323227325231}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: 'This renders VR 180 stereoscopic format by first rendering cubemaps
    with the left and right eye cameras, converting these images to fisheye using
    a specialized shader, and then combining them into a double wide side-by-side
    stereoscopic final image.


    To preserve HDR quality floating space render
    textures are recommended.


    To use this setup in your own scene, simply add
    this prefab in place of your camera. The examples are configured to render 2K
    which you may customize. Make sure changes to the render resolution match the
    render textures in use, or errors may occur.'
  Warning: "Certain rendering features such as screen space effects, some shaders,
    and post processing filters may not be supported in this rendering setup and
    may result in rendering anomalies. To avoid these issues, test early on and decide
    on rendering features that work with cubemap rendering. \n\nThe shader is based
    on the Fulldome Camera for Unity package available on GitHub and has been included
    in Timeflow under the MIT License.\n\nLayer Masks\nThe built-in 'Ignore Raycast'
    layer is used to separate the rendering of the MainCamera from the post processing
    camera, volume, and image plane. Note also that the MainCamera exlcudes the 'Ignore
    Raycast' layer in its culling mask so that it doesn't render the image plane.\n\nYou
    may change the layer to any that works best for your project, though make sure
    that both the Culling Mask and Volume Mask on the cameras are set to match the
    layer assigned, otherwise you may not get the results desired."
  URLTitle: Rendering Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/rendering
  URL2Title: Fulldome Camera for Unity
  URL2: https://github.com/rsodre/FulldomeCameraForUnity
